"Aaron Rodgers' 2026 NFL season: Tracking records, milestones","description":"The Pittsburgh passer is chasing records in his 22nd NFL season, and ESPN is chronicling his \"last rodeo.\"","published":"2026-11-16T06:36:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/49907062/aaron-rodgers-2026-nfl-season-steelers-packers-jets-tracking-records-milestones","type":"Story","byline":"Brooke Pryor","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 10 winners and losers: McCaffrey, Gibbs and Mahomes dominate Sunday","description":"Christian McCafffrey, Jahmyr Gibbs and Patrick Mahomes put fantasy teams on their back in Week 10, while Jonathan Taylor and the Packers and Panthers' passing games had quiet days.","published":"2026-11-16T05:17:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/page/FFSundayHighLows-50494331/nfl-week-10-fantasy-football-winners-losers-injuries-rankings-more","type":"Story","byline":"Matt Bowen and Tristan H. Cockcroft","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Fantasy buzz: Week 10's leading scorers through 'Sunday Night Football'","description":"Kansas City rookie Emmett Johnson stepped in for Kenneth Walker III and was one of the top fantasy scorers of Week 10.","published":"2026-11-16T05:07:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/40699880/fantasy-football-injuries-position-battles-nfl-news-analysis","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN Fantasy","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 10 NFL highlights: Best plays, moments, touchdowns, more","description":"Check here for all of Sunday's top moments, TDs and analysis from ESPN's NFL reporters.","published":"2026-11-16T05:24:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50489998/week-10-highlights-sunday-best-plays-touchdowns-2026","type":"Story","byline":"NFL Nation","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Aaron Rodgers makes fantasy football history, now No. 2 on all-time scoring list","description":"With Aaron Rodgers' score on Sunday, he reaches another fantasy football accolade in his HOF-worthy career.","published":"2026-11-16T04:27:04.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/50328859/fantasy-football-aaron-rodgers-career-points-scoring","type":"Story","byline":"Tristan H. Cockcroft","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"49ers put up big numbers vs. Cowboys, tout 'incredibly dangerous' offense","description":"The 49ers racked up 584 yards against the Cowboys on Sunday in a jaw-dropping offensive display led by Brock Purdy, Christian McCaffrey and Deebo Samuel.","published":"2026-11-16T05:29:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50498373/49ers-put-big-numbers-victory-cowboys","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Nick Wagoner","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Jaxon Smith-Njigba's 144-yard quarter sparks Seahawks in win over Raiders","description":"Jaxon Smith-Njigba, the NFL's leading receiver, finished with a season-high 171 yards on eight catches, with 144 coming in the third quarter to help the Seahawks turn a three-point halftime deficit into a 21-13 win over the Raiders on Sunday.","published":"2026-11-16T04:43:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50498326/jaxon-smith-njigba-144-yard-third-quarter-sparks-seahawks-offense-win-raiders","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Brady Henderson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Schottenheimer 'very disappointed, very frustrated' with Cowboys' porous defense","description":"Brian Schottenheimer said the Cowboys' defensive performance in the second half was a first for him after it gave up nearly 600 yards to the 49ers.","published":"2026-11-16T03:55:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50498058/schottenheimer-very-frustrated-porous-cowboys-defense","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Todd Archer","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Tay Martin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tay_Martin","description":"American football player (born 1997)","touched":"2026-11-15T08:36:41Z","intro":"Davontavean Martin (born December 14, 1997) is an American professional football wide receiver for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Washington State Cougars and Oklahoma State Cowboys. Martin has also been a member of the San Francisco 49ers, Tennessee Titans, Washington Commanders, and the UFL's Columbus Aviators. He was signed as an undrafted free agent by the 49ers following the 2022 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"SAN FRANCISCO 49ERS\nOn April 30, 2022, Martin signed with the San Francisco 49ers as an undrafted free agent. He was released during final roster cutdowns on August 30. Martin was signed to the team's practice squad the following day. He signed a reserve/future contract with the 49ers on January 31, 2023.\nOn August 29, 2023, Martin was waived by the 49ers and re-signed to the practice squad. He signed a reserve/future contract with San Francisco on February 13, 2024.\nMartin was waived by the 49ers on August 27, 2024, and re-signed to the practice squad. On September 3, Martin was released from the practice squad.\n\nTENNESSEE TITANS\nOn September 10, 2024, Martin was signed to the Tennessee Titans' practice squad. He was promoted to the active roster on January 4, 2025. In a 23-14 Week 18 loss to the Houston Texans, Martin made his first career reception on a 49-yard touchdown pass from quarterback Will Levis.\nOn May 7, 2025, Martin was waived/injured by the Titans and reverted to the injured reserve the following day. He was waived again on May 14.\n\nWASHINGTON COMMANDERS\nMartin signed with the Washington Commanders on July 23, 2025, and was released on August 26. Martin re-signed with their practice squad on September 16. He was elevated to the active roster for Weeks 4, 5, and 6, but was released from the practice squad on October 17.\n\nCOLUMBUS AVIATORS\nOn January 14, 2026, Martin was selected by the Columbus Aviators of the United Football League (UFL).\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn June 16, 2026, Martin signed with the Detroit Lions. For his contributions to special teams in the Week 1 win against the Saints, he received a game ball."},{"key":"personal","title":"Personal life","text":"Tay Martin is engaged to Morgan Pitre. They have two daughters, Reign and Valley."}],"wikidataId":"Q114282822","social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-07-22","text":"Waived WR Kyre Duplessis. Signed WRs Tarik Black, Lucky Jackson and Tay Martin to contracts. Placed WR Kendrick Law on injured reserve."},{"date":"2026-06-16","text":"Signed WRs Tay Martin, Tarik Black and Lucky Jackson to contracts. Placed WR Kendrick Law on injured reserve. Waived WR Kyre Duplessis."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4245144","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/M/MartTa00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/tay-martin/61811","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/tay-martin/10555","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tay_Martin"},"insights":["2026 cap number of $1.0M is the 44th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Entered the league in 2022 as an undrafted free agent."]}